<title>SWITZERLAND: CSFB lifts earnings estimates for Baer.</title>
<headline>CSFB lifts earnings estimates for Baer.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Suisse First Boston said it had raised its earnings estimates and share price target for Bank Julius Baer because booming financial markets should produce more commission income than orginally expected.</p>
<p>It raised its 12-month share price target to 1,900 Swiss francs from 1,720 and gave these EPS estimates:</p>
<p>				     1996 actual  1997	 1998</p>
<p> Annual EPS (Sfr)		111.2	  124.1	132.1</p>
<p> P/E				 11.9	   14.2	 13.3</p>
<p> Net profit (million Sfr)	  131.0	  150.2	164.3</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
